# RectangleStencil

`RectangleStencil` is the default stencil of [`Cropper`](/docs/components/Cropper) and [`FixedCropper`](/docs/components/FixedCropper): a rectangle with eight resize handlers and four draggable edges, which the user can move by dragging its inside. It supports a fixed or a ranged aspect ratio and an optional grid.

The cropper renders the stencil itself, so you don't place it in your markup. Configure it through the cropper's `stencilProps`:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { Cropper } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';
</script>

<Cropper {src} stencilProps={{ aspectRatio: 16 / 9, grid: true }} />
```

Inside, the stencil is built from [`StencilWrapper`](/docs/components/StencilWrapper), [`BoundingBox`](/docs/components/BoundingBox) (resizing), [`DraggableArea`](/docs/components/DraggableArea) (moving), [`StencilOverlay`](/docs/components/StencilOverlay) (the darkened surroundings) and `StencilGrid`. It renders nothing until the cropper has a state.

## Props

### `aspectRatio`

**Type:** `number | { minimum?: number; maximum?: number }`

The aspect ratio (width divided by height) of the crop area. A number fixes it, and an object allows a range. By default the ratio is free. See [Set the aspect ratio](/docs/guides/recipes#set-the-aspect-ratio).

### `minAspectRatio`

**Type:** `number`

The lowest allowed aspect ratio. It is ignored when `aspectRatio` is set.

### `maxAspectRatio`

**Type:** `number`

The highest allowed aspect ratio. It is ignored when `aspectRatio` is set.

### `movable`

**Type:** `boolean` · **Default:** `true`

Whether the user can move the stencil by dragging it.

### `resizable`

**Type:** `boolean` · **Default:** `true`

Whether the user can resize the stencil with its handlers and lines.

### `grid`

**Type:** `boolean` · **Default:** `false`

Draws a 3×3 grid inside the stencil while the user interacts with the cropper. It becomes a finer 9×9 grid while the image is being rotated. See [Add the grid](/docs/guides/recipes#add-the-grid).

### `coordinates`

**Type:** `Coordinates | ((state: CropperState | null) => Coordinates)`

Where to draw the stencil, in boundary pixels. By default it follows the crop area (`getStencilCoordinates(state)`). Override it only when your cropper shows the stencil somewhere else than the crop area.

### `class`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes for the stencil's root element. This is upstream's `className`.

### `movingClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes added to the root element while the user moves the stencil.

### `resizingClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes added to the root element while the user resizes the stencil.

### `previewClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes for the preview element, the transparent area inside the stencil. Use it to draw a border or a mask shape. See [Customize Appearance](/docs/guides/customize-appearance#preview).

### `overlayClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes for the overlay that darkens everything outside the stencil. Its `color` sets the shade. See [Customize Appearance](/docs/guides/customize-appearance#overlay).

### `gridClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes for the grid, when `grid` is on.

### `boundingBoxClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes for the bounding box that holds the handlers and lines. You will rarely need it.

### `draggableAreaClassName`

**Type:** `ClassValue`

Classes for the draggable area that moves the stencil.

### `handlerComponent`

**Type:** `Component` · **Default:** `SimpleHandler`

The component drawn for each handler. It receives the props listed in [`SimpleHandler`](/docs/components/SimpleHandler#props).

### `handlers`

**Type:** `Partial<Record<OrdinalDirection, boolean>>` · **Default:** all eight `true`

```ts
interface Handlers {
	eastNorth?: boolean;
	north?: boolean;
	westNorth?: boolean;
	west?: boolean;
	westSouth?: boolean;
	south?: boolean;
	eastSouth?: boolean;
	east?: boolean;
}
```

Which handlers to show. Only the keys set to `true` are drawn, so this shows the corner handlers alone:

```ts
const handlers = { eastNorth: true, westNorth: true, westSouth: true, eastSouth: true };
```

Pass `{}` to hide every handler. Through `stencilProps`, `false` and `true` also work, and hide or show them all.

### `handlerClassNames`

**Type:** `HandlerClassNames`

```ts
interface HandlerClassNames {
	default?: ClassValue;
	hover?: ClassValue;
	disabled?: ClassValue;
	eastNorth?: ClassValue;
	north?: ClassValue;
	westNorth?: ClassValue;
	west?: ClassValue;
	westSouth?: ClassValue;
	south?: ClassValue;
	eastSouth?: ClassValue;
	east?: ClassValue;
}
```

Classes for the handler elements. `default` goes on every handler, each direction key on that handler only, and `hover` on a handler while the pointer is over it. `disabled` is accepted but not applied, as in react-advanced-cropper. See [Customize the classnames](/docs/guides/customize-appearance#customize-the-classnames).

### `handlerWrapperClassNames`

**Type:** `HandlerClassNames`

Classes for the wrappers around the handlers (the larger, invisible hit areas). `default` and the direction keys are applied. `hover` and `disabled` are accepted but not applied.

### `lineComponent`

**Type:** `Component` · **Default:** `SimpleLine`

The component drawn for each edge. It receives the props listed in [`SimpleLine`](/docs/components/SimpleLine#props).

### `lines`

**Type:** `Partial<Record<CardinalDirection, boolean>>` · **Default:** all four `true`

```ts
interface Lines {
	north?: boolean;
	west?: boolean;
	south?: boolean;
	east?: boolean;
}
```

Which edges are drawn and can be dragged to resize the stencil. For example, `{ north: true, south: true }` keeps only the top and bottom edges. As with `handlers`, a boolean through `stencilProps` toggles them all.

### `lineClassNames`

**Type:** `LineClassNames`

```ts
interface LineClassNames {
	default?: ClassValue;
	hover?: ClassValue;
	disabled?: ClassValue;
	north?: ClassValue;
	west?: ClassValue;
	south?: ClassValue;
	east?: ClassValue;
}
```

Classes for the line elements: `default` on every line, a direction key on that line, `hover` while the pointer is over it, and `disabled` while resizing is off.

### `lineWrapperClassNames`

**Type:** `LineClassNames`

Classes for the wrappers around the lines (their hit areas). `default`, `disabled` and the direction keys are applied. `hover` is accepted but not applied.

## Service props

<Admonition type="danger" title="Remember">

Don't pass these yourself. The cropper passes them to the stencil, and its values win over `stencilProps`.

</Admonition>

### `cropper`

**Type:** `CropperRef`

The [cropper](/docs/components/Cropper#methods) that owns the stencil. The stencil reads the state, transitions and interactions from it, and calls `moveCoordinates` and `resizeCoordinates` when the user drags.

### `image`

**Type:** `CropperImage | null`

```ts
interface CropperImage {
	src: string;
	revoke: boolean;
	transforms: Transforms;
	arrayBuffer: ArrayBuffer | null;
	width: number;
	height: number;
}
```

The current image. `RectangleStencil` doesn't use it, but custom stencils may.

### `disabled`

**Type:** `boolean`

The cropper's `disabled` prop. A disabled stencil can't be moved or resized.

## Exports

The cropper binds the stencil with `bind:this` and passes its exports to `stencilConstraints`. That is how the stencil's aspect ratio reaches the cropper settings.

| Export        | Type                                     | Description                                                                                 |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `aspectRatio` | `{ minimum: number; maximum: number }`   | `aspectRatio`, or `minAspectRatio` and `maxAspectRatio`, normalized into a range. Read-only. |

React exposes the same value through the stencil's ref (`useImperativeHandle`). A [custom stencil](/docs/tutorials/custom-stencil) can export its own options the same way.

## CSS classes

| Element          | Classes                                                                                                                                                |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Root             | `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil`, plus `advanced-cropper-stencil-wrapper` and `advanced-cropper-artificial-transition` from `StencilWrapper`       |
| Root modifiers   | `--movable` and `--resizable` (when allowed), `--moving` and `--resizing` (during the interaction), `--disabled`                                        |
| Bounding box     | `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__bounding-box`                                                                                                     |
| Draggable area   | `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__draggable-area`                                                                                                   |
| Overlay          | `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__overlay`                                                                                                          |
| Grid             | `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__grid`                                                                                                             |
| Preview          | `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__preview`                                                                                                          |

The modifiers are written in full, for example `advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil--moving`. Only `--movable` has a base style (the move cursor); the others are hooks for themes and your own CSS.
